  "articleHtml": "<main>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cafe Rio Calories Calculator\n    </span>\n</p>\n<div>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n      Meta Title:\n     </span>\n<span>\n      Cafe Rio Calories Calculator: Nutrition &amp; Macros\n     </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n      Meta Description:\n     </span>\n<span>\n      Calculate Cafe Rio calories, protein, carbs, fat, and sodium for burritos, salads, bowls, tacos, tortillas, meats, rice, beans, sauces, and dressings.\n     </span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.8n72z1xou6m1\">\n<span>\n     Cafe Rio Calories Calculator\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     At Cafe Rio, a burrito, salad, or bowl is really a combination of several ingredients. Your tortilla, rice, beans, protein, cheese, guacamole, sauce, and dressing can each change the final nutrition.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Use the\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Cafe Rio Calories Calculator above\n    </span>\n<span>\n     to build an order that matches what you actually eat and see the combined calories, protein, carbohydrates, fat, sodium, and other available nutrition values.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.vhcyuoeca0sg\">\n<span>\n     Calculate the Ingredients Inside Your Order\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     There is no single calorie number that accurately describes every Cafe Rio burrito or salad.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A typical order can be built from several components:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Tortilla\n     <br/>\n     Cilantro lime rice\n     <br/>\n     Black or pinto beans\n     <br/>\n     Protein\n     <br/>\n     Cheese and toppings\n     <br/>\n     Sauce or dressing\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Changing even one of these ingredients changes the finished meal.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For the most useful estimate, recreate your order from the individual components instead of relying on a generic burrito, salad, or bowl value.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.r898cjggy0o1\">\n<span>\n     The Tortilla Can Be a Significant Part of a Burrito\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cafe Rio is known for its fresh-made tortillas, and the tortilla itself contributes a meaningful amount to a burrito's nutrition.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     NutritionSolver currently lists a\n    </span>\n<span>\n     12-inch flour tortilla at 420 calories\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , while smaller corn and flour tortillas have much lower totals.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     That means switching from a large burrito tortilla to tacos or another format can change the meal before rice, beans, meat, or toppings are even added.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Always select the tortilla that matches your actual order.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.mf2gpgsu8ri\">\n<span>\n     Rice and Beans Add More Than Carbohydrates\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cilantro lime rice and beans are common building blocks in Cafe Rio meals.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The current database lists\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Cilantro Lime Rice at 110 calories\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , while Black Beans and Pinto Beans provide both carbohydrates and protein along with notable amounts of fiber.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Beans therefore should not be viewed as only a carbohydrate ingredient.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If your order includes both rice and beans, add both components. If you ask for extra rice or double beans, the final nutrition will increase accordingly.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.234go169gex2\">\n<span>\n     Sweet Pork Has a Different Macro Profile From Other Proteins\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cafe Rio's\n    </span>\n<span>\n     Sweet Pork Barbacoa\n    </span>\n<span>\n     is one of the brand's signature ingredients, but it does not have the same nutrition profile as grilled chicken or steak.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Its sweet preparation contributes carbohydrates and sugar in addition to protein and fat.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Other protein choices, including Fire-Grilled Chicken, Fire-Grilled Steak, Pollo Asado, Shredded Chicken Breast, and seafood options, have different balances of calories and macros.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If protein is important to your comparison, check the\n    </span>\n<span>\n     protein amount alongside calories, carbs, fat, and sodium\n    </span>\n<span>\n     rather than choosing by meat type alone.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.dmtqvgt8guhg\">\n<span>\n     Salad Dressing Can Change the Final Total\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     A Cafe Rio salad includes many of the same ingredients found in other entr\u00e9es, and the dressing can make a noticeable difference.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For example, the current NutritionSolver data lists:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Creamy Tomatillo Dressing:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     150 calories and 15g fat\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cilantro Lime Dressing:\n    </span>\n<span>\n     130 calories with a different carbohydrate and fat profile\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The dressing should therefore be included when calculating the full salad.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If you use only part of the serving, your actual intake will be lower than the full listed portion.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.v8250xuy8eq6\">\n<span>\n     Enchilada Style Adds Another Layer\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cafe Rio burritos can be ordered\n    </span>\n<span>\n     enchilada style\n    </span>\n<span>\n     , adding sauce and other toppings to the finished burrito.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     That means a standard handheld burrito and an enchilada-style burrito should not automatically share the same calorie total.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Start with the burrito ingredients, then include the sauce, cheese, or other additions that come with the preparation you choose.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     This ingredient-by-ingredient approach makes customized orders much easier to estimate.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.36q2r66pjx10\">\n<span>\n     Chips, Queso, and Guacamole Belong in the Full Order\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Chips and dips are separate from the entr\u00e9e.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     If your meal includes:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Burrito + chips + queso\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     or\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Salad + chips + guacamole\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     the nutrition of the chips and dip should be added to the entr\u00e9e total.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The same rule applies to extra guacamole, sour cream, tortilla strips, salsa, and additional sauces.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Small extras can become meaningful when several are added to the same meal.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.irsyk23h771s\">\n<span>\n     Drinks and Desserts Count Separately\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Cafe Rio also offers drinks and desserts such as specialty beverages, horchata, limeade, Tres Leches, and Fresh Lime Pie.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     These are not part of the nutrition of your burrito, salad, or bowl unless a combined meal entry specifically says otherwise.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     For a complete calculation, think in terms of:\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Entr\u00e9e + extras + drink + dessert\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     rather than stopping at the main item.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.fh22oqfuqlu7\">\n<span>\n     Cafe Rio Nutrition Questions\n    </span>\n</h2><div class=\"faq-accordion-container space-y-3 my-6\"><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>How many calories are in a Cafe Rio burrito?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>How can I calculate Cafe Rio Sweet Pork calories?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Is a Cafe Rio salad automatically lower in calories than a burrito?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Does Cafe Rio dressing add calories?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Should I count guacamole and sour cream separately?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details><details class=\"faq-accordion-item glass-card-static rounded-xl border border-zinc-800/80 p-0 mb-3 overflow-hidden group\"><summary class=\"faq-accordion-summary font-bold text-white text-sm md:text-base cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between p-4 bg-zinc-900/60 hover:bg-zinc-900 transition-colors\"><span>Why can Cafe Rio nutrition vary?</span><span>+</span></summary><div class=\"faq-accordion-answer p-4 text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/40\"></div></details></div>\n<h2 class=\"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-8 pb-2 border-b border-emerald-500/20 flex items-center gap-2.5\" id=\"h.nyxqaco5kqgy\">\n<span>\n     Build the Cafe Rio Meal You Actually Eat\n    </span>\n</h2>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     The most useful Cafe Rio nutrition number is not an average burrito or salad calorie count. It is the total from the\n    </span>\n<span>\n     specific ingredients in your own order\n    </span>\n<span>\n     .\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     Select your tortilla or entr\u00e9e format, then add rice, beans, protein, toppings, sauces, dressing, sides, and drinks as needed.\n    </span>\n</p>\n<p class=\"text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-4\">\n<span>\n     NutritionSolver combines those available values so you can compare complete Cafe Rio orders without doing the nutrition math manually.\n    </span>\n</p>\n</main>",
  "seoTitle": "Cafe Rio Calories Calculator: Nutrition & Macros",
  "seoDescription": "Calculate Cafe Rio calories, protein, carbs, fat, and sodium for burritos, salads, bowls, tacos, tortillas, meats, rice, beans, sauces, and dressings.",
  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "How many calories are in a Cafe Rio burrito?",
      "a": "There is no single calorie amount for every Cafe Rio burrito. The total depends on the tortilla, rice, beans, protein, cheese, sauces, guacamole, and other ingredients you choose."
    },
    {
      "q": "How can I calculate Cafe Rio Sweet Pork calories?",
      "a": "Add the Sweet Pork Barbacoa portion together with the tortilla, rice, beans, sauces, and toppings in your actual order. Sweet Pork by itself is only one component of the finished entr\u00e9e."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is a Cafe Rio salad automatically lower in calories than a burrito?",
      "a": "Not necessarily. A salad can include a tortilla, rice, beans, protein, cheese, guacamole, tortilla strips, and dressing. The complete ingredient combination determines the final total."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does Cafe Rio dressing add calories?",
      "a": "Yes. Dressings have their own calories and macros and should be added when calculating a salad."
    },
    {
      "q": "Should I count guacamole and sour cream separately?",
      "a": "Yes, when they are listed as separate components. Include any extras that match your actual order."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why can Cafe Rio nutrition vary?",
      "a": "Customizations, ingredient portions, recipe updates, and menu changes can alter the final nutrition. Published restaurant values represent standard portions and should be used as estimates."
    }
  ]
}